/**
 * What a program asks about the machine it runs on (docs/design/OS.md). Today it is the skeleton of the package: the
 * three target constants of `std/core`, re-exported so that a file that branches on the system writes one import, and
 * the raw layer of one `native type` per family of systems in a directory of its own.
 *
 * A branch on the system is a `match OperatingSystem.current`: every arm is type checked on every machine, and only the
 * arm of the build's target is compiled. So a call of the Windows layer belongs in a `.Windows` arm, and
 * `torb check --every-target` reports one that is reached on another system.
 *
 * # Examples
 *
 *     fn pathListSeparator(): String {
 *       match OperatingSystem.current {
 *         .Windows => ";"
 *         .Linux | .MacOs | .FreeBsd => ":"
 *       }
 *     }
 *
 * # Related
 *
 * - [OperatingSystem] - the constant a branch reads, with the cases every branch handles.
 */

public use OperatingSystem, Architecture, ByteOrder from "std/core"
